  "historical_output_text": " I just realized all the clothes hanging up after washing are wrinkly. Why did it happen even I dried and stored all the laundry in my usual spot, but didn’t change my dryer settings. It’s so inconvenient.\n\nWrinkleness can occur during and/or right as after the clothes have left out the dry cleaning. This can occur because:\n1- Over-detergency, which means clothes were dried with excess laundry detergency\nor,\n  a - The clothes might have absorbed too high amount water during cleaning, making them extra sensitive.\n2-Dryers have settings and temperatures which work for most fabrics, some settings work only well with lighter clothes.\nSo it would make a sense to first make some small checks on:\n1) Did you wash with a good quality liquid laundry detergent instead of a gel, as they are often stronger?\n    ",
